From: "YES Linux Release Team" <release@yeslinux.org>
Date: 2005/02/03 Thu AM 11:27:12 GMT+05:30
To: news@yeslinux.org
Subject: YES Linux 2.1 Build 1 available now!

YES Corporation would like to announce the immediate availability of YES
Linux 2.1 Build 1.  We are very excited about this release because for the
first time we feature Virtual Host support.  User have the option of using
either a one step Web Based or a one step commandline interface.  Using
either interface the Virtual Hosting System allows for the creation,
enabling, or disabling of Virtual Hosts in a completely modular
configuration.  This means that no two Virtual Hosts share a configuration
information, making maintance of each Virtual Host easiler and have a
lower cost.  We have fixed a configuration bug that affected
authentication using WebDav.  Now WebDav authenticates properly for both
the primary website and all virtual hosts.  We have created more
documentation for YES Linux available from
http://www.yeslinux.org/docs.php. We have upgraded SquirrelMail to the
latest edition, standardize on website naming convention, and Cleaned up
the extra directories associated with Apache.

In adition to the above changes the YES Linux Configuration system now
supports a dynamic message bus, allowing for dynamic events to be fired. 
This means that administrators and thirdparty developers no longer have to
edit build files, they now have a choice.  They can use the existing
method or they can create an Event (Directory) and place an unlimited
number of build files in that directory.  Then once the driver task is
executed all the build files for that Event are dynamically loaded and
executed sequentially (Determined by the Number prefixing the build file
name with lower values having precedence).

We expect to have one final release of YES Linux 2.1 that will include web
statistics for each virtual host created.  After that we will begin work
on YES Linux 2.2.

YES Linux can be downloaded from

    * http://www.yeslinux.org/iso/
    * BitTorrent Network http://www.tlm-project.org/torrents/yeslinux
    * Our mirrors http://www.yeslinux.org/iso/mirrors.php

A list of installed applications are available at
http://www.yeslinux.org/forum/viewtopic.php?p=997#1050.

The major changes YES Linux 2.1.1:
--------------------------
addition:
yes-configuration - added message bus task.  This task is the base for the
dynamic message bus
yes-configuration - added tags for Virtual Hosting

-------------------------
updates:
squirrelmail to latest version
yes-configuration build file to use default ant tasks
yes-configuration - updated configuration to use default ant symlink task
yes-configuration - updated AntAdapter to use new ProjectHelper discovery
pattern
yes-intro - updated to add virtual hosting initial setup
yes-rebrand - removed custom link class to use default ant symlink task
yes-website - added virtual hosting admin
yes-security - added support for virtual hosting admin
yes-boot - rebranded for YES Linux
yes-administration - added webadmin, fixed webdav authentication
made website directories consistent /site/docs and /site/cgi-bin

-------------------------
removals:
yes-configuration - removed custom XSL ant task because ant already has one

Sincerely,
YES Corporation
