In case you had given up on the linux-india.org site, then please take a second 
look. Raju Mathur of Delhi has given it a new lease of life, by making it a 
very collaborative project.

 	See http://www.linux-india.org

As he puts it: This site is for you, the Linux user in India! You can use the 
resources on this site to:

     * Get access to the latest Linux/FLOSS news in India
     * Create and publish your own web site
     * Get a quick look at upcoming Liunux/FLOSS events
     * Search for jobs (and people appropriate for jobs)
     * Find a Linux User Group (LUG) near you
     * ...and much more

Please create an account and edit your personal page to get a feel of what can 
be done with this site.  The only tools you need are this browser, your mouse 
and your keyboard.

If you would like to submit news (about FLOSS in your region) or announce any 
upcoming event, and if you're having a difficulty in doing so, just email me a 
copy. I've volunteered to help with the news pages; you too can similarly 
support some other section.

We all *do* need a national network to share links and information! FN
